n of a split read against the implied junction.\n\n    Colinear model: read prefix maps at s1, suffix maps so that read offset\n    off2 lands at ref position p2. Implied deletion size D = p2 - off2 - s1.\n    Returns (ok, del_start_lo, del_start_hi, D) where [del_start_lo,\n    del_start_hi) is the range of possible left breakpoints (1-based style\n    handled by caller; here 0-based ref coords).\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    D = p2 - off2 - s1\n    if D <= READ_LEN:\n        return False, -1, -1, D\n    need = s1 + D + READ_LEN\n    if need > len(refc):\n        return False, -1, -1, D\n    m1 = readc \"'!= refc[s1:s1 + READ_LEN]\n    m2 = readc != refc[s1 + D:s1 + D + READ_LEN]\n    a = int(np.argmax(m1)) if m1.any() else READ_LEN   # prefix matches [0, a)\n    if not m2.any():\n        b = READ_LEN\n    else:\n        b = READ_LEN - int(np.argmax(m2[::-1]))          # suffix matches [b, L)\n    if a >= b:  # a consistent crossover t exists in [b, a]\n        return True, s1 + b, s1 + a + 1, D\n    return False, -1, -1, D\n'\"'@\nAdd-Content -LiteralPath output\\\\analysis.py -Value \"'$part2 -Encoding utf8\nWrite-Host \"part2 appended, lines: $((Get-Content output'\"\\\\analysis.py).Count)\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"part2 appended, lines: 265\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"reasoning","text":"OK, Part 3: depth analysis, discordant pairs, integration, output writing, and main. Let's write this carefully.\n\nDepth computation:\n- Use primary alignments of reads with support>=2 and status in (UNIQUE, SPLIT) (count once per read).\n- Bin starts into FINE_BIN bins: np.bincount(starts // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbins).\n- Mappable bp per fine bin: bincount of positions where codes != 4. But edge effect: a read start at position p covers [p, p+150); near N gaps, reads can't fully map. As an approximation, mappable bp based on ACGT content is enough for our purpose (we also report the depth ratio).\n\nActually a better normalization for expected depth: for each fine bin, expected counts ∝ number of valid start positions = number of positions p in the bin such that the reference [p, p+READ_LEN) is entirely ACGT. Compute with a sliding window validity: valid_start[p] = all(codes[p:p+READ_LEN] != 4). Vectorize: use min over windows via cumulative count of non-ACGT: bad_cum; valid[p] = bad_cum[p+READ_LEN] - bad_cum[p] == 0. Then bincount the valid positions per bin. This is accurate and cheap. Normalize depth_cn[b] = (reads_b / valid_b) / (total_reads_used / total_valid).\n\n- 100kb cn: aggregate fine bins (sum of reads, sum of valid).\n\nCall detection:\n- Compute median cn over bins with valid_bp > 50% of bin size (i.e., mappable bins). Should be ~1.0 by construction (since we normalize by global mean) — actually normalize so global mean = 1.0; per-bin cn fluctuates with Poisson noise: mean reads per 100kb bin = depth 2x → 100kb×2/300… wait, reads: expected reads per 100kb = coverage×bin/READ_LEN? no: number of read starts per bp ≈ coverage/fragment_length ≈ 2/300 ≈ 0.0067 → per 100kb ≈ 667 reads per mate… both mates counted: ~1333 reads/bin. Poisson noise σ≈36 → ~2.7% — very clean signal.\n\n- Find candidate runs of consecutive big bins with cn < 0.35 (homozygous-like) — also compute 0.35-0.7 as heterozygous. Select the longest run by size. Also require the run to have length ≥ 3 bins (300kb) to qualify as \"large\".\n\nBoundary refinement at fine bins: scan outward from run core: find contiguous fine bins with cn < 0.35 (or < 0.5×flank median), extending from the big-bin run. Define depth_start = first reduced fine bin position; depth_end = (last reduced fine bin + 1) × FINE_BIN.\n\nDiscordant pairs:\n- Both mates UNIQUE/SPLIT with support ≥2; require status != AMBIG for both mates; FR: strand1=+1, strand2=-1, start2 >= start1; span = start2 + READ_LEN - start1.\n- Insert distribution from spans < 2000 (to exclude spanning pairs): median, MAD.\n- Threshold T = max(2000, median + 8*MAD). Discordant = FR pairs with span >= T. Also collect RF/FF/RR anomalies but don't use for deletion (report counts).\n- For discordant pairs, midpoint = start1 + (start2 + READ_LEN - start1)/2 … for a spanning pair, breakpoints: left breakpoint ≈ start1 + READ_LEN/2 (roughly within the fragment), more precisely, given fixed fragment length F: left_breakpoint ∈ [start1, start1+F]… deletion D = span - F. For each spanning pair, D_est = span - median_insert. Breakpoint window: the left breakpoint lies within [start1, start1 + READ_LEN] hmm, actually: mate1 covers [start1, start1+150), mate2 covers [start2, start2+150). The fragment is mate1_start .. mate2_end with two breakpoints… in the case of a deletion, the fragment aligns as: [start1, start1+x) then jumps to [y, y+(F-x)), where y-x = D. Mate1 = first 150bp of the fragment → if x >= 150, mate1 lies entirely to the left of the breakpoint: start1+150 <= breakpoint_left… mate2 is the last 150bp. So the breakpoint lies within (start1+150 - ... , ...): we know left_breakpoint >= start1+150 - (F - 150)? For F≈300: mate1 (150bp) + mate2 (150bp) nearly tile the entire fragment; if the breakpoint falls between them, we get discordance. Constraints: left_bp > start1 (mate1 must map entirely left) and left_bp < start1 + F - 150 + … anyway the window width is ~F-150 ≈ 150-300bp. Midpoint-based estimate: left_bp ≈ start1 + F/2 ± F/2. For reporting, the cluster of midpoints of spanning pairs gives the breakpoint region to ~1kb with enough pairs. Good enough as \"spanning evidence\"; split reads are better.\n\nSplit reads:\n- For reads with status SPLIT: verify with verify_split_junction(refc, readc[i], s1, s2, off2, p2). Collect verified junctions: left breakpoint range [lo, hi) and D. Cluster by (approx left_breakpoint, D): group junctions whose lo is within 50bp and D within 50bp of each other.\n- refined_start = cluster's breakpoint lo (0-based) → 1-based coordinate: left breakpoint = the last retained base is s1+b (0-based), first deleted base is s1+b+1 (1-based)… define 1-based: left_break_1based = s1 + b + 1? hmm. Let me define in 0-based half-open: deleted interval [B1, B2) with B2-B1 = D. Then 1-based closed form: first deleted base = B1+1, last deleted base = B2. For the TSV we round anyway; for the report, give 1-based inclusive coordinates: start = B1+1, end = B2.\n\nIntegration:\n- If there are verified split-read clusters: refined_start = B1+1 (1-based), refined_end = B2. Prefer clusters with most support; if multiple clusters (multiple junctions, e.g., complex), take extremes? For a single deletion, expect one cluster (possibly 2-4 reads).\n- elif discordant pairs: refined_start = min midpoint (1-based), refined_end = max midpoint; note precision ±insert.\n- else depth boundaries: refined_start = depth_start+1, refined_end = depth_end (fine-bin precision).\n\nConsistency check: refined breakpoints should be near depth boundaries (within ~100kb); otherwise note in the report.\n\nAlso depth inside/outside: mean cn of big bins inside the run vs outside (mappable bins).\n\nsupporting_signals string, e.g.:\n`read_depth=<n>x100kb_bins_at_<cn_in>x_vs_<cn_out>x;discordant_pairs=<k>(span~<d>bp);split_reads=<m>`\n\nWrite TSV, JSON, and report.\n\nMain(): orchestrate everything, time it, write outputs. Dump depth profile of candidate regions (fine bins) to qc.json as well (for transparency).\n\nAlso QC JSON: per-signal counts, thresholds used, insert stats, alignment stats, mappability.\n\nOK let's write Part 3. Note: in align_reads, AMBIG is set only when c1==1 and the second best is also ==1 — but the case c1==1 with len(ranked)==1 (single unique seed hit) is: does it fall through to UNIQUE with support 1? Look at the code: if c1==1 and len(ranked)>1 and ranked[1][1]==1 → AMBIG. Otherwise strand/start/support get set; status=UNIQUE with support 1. Hmm — single-seed support alignment is risky (may be a spurious repetitive hit that was masked out… we capped mult at 16, so a seed with 5 hits gives 5 candidate starts each with support 1). For depth counting, use only support>=2. But we mark status UNIQUE — should distinguish. Let's add: status = UNIQUE if c1 >= 2, else keep support=1 (still call it UNIQUE but support reflects it; downstream filters on support>=2). That's fine — downstream uses support>=2.\n\nAlso SPLIT detection requires st2 == st1 and abs(s2-s1) > READ_LEN. Deletion split reads: same strand, far apart. Good. But wait — the secondary cluster with c2 == 1 (a single seed): abs(s2-s1) > 150. A true split read: 2 seeds left + 1 seed right. Good. However, if the primary c1==1 (1 seed left) and secondary is also 1 seed, this becomes AMBIG and we miss the split read. For junction verification, we need the left start anyway — the single-seed left start could be verified by the junction check itself (if the junction verifies with a consistent crossover, the whole alignment is confirmed). But my code discards AMBIG before the split check. Improvement: even in AMBIG (all clusters support 1), if there are exactly 2 clusters on the same strand with |s2-s1| > READ_LEN → mark SPLIT (will be verified at the base level later). Let's patch Part 2… rewrite that section. Easier to append a fix? no — the align loop is already written. I can edit the file later with a small python patch, or incorporate into Part 3 as a monkey-patch? Cleaner: after writing Part 3, use a small python replace to fix that block in the file. Let's plan the exact replacement text.\n\nCurrent block:\n```python\n        ranked = sorted(best.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))\n        (st1, s1), c1 = ranked[0]\n        if c1 == 1 and len(ranked) > 1 and ranked[1][1] == 1:\n            status[i] = AMBIG          # no locus has >= 2 seeds\n            continue\n```\nReplace with:\n```python\n        ranked = sorted(best.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))\n        (st1, s1), c1 = ranked[0]\n        if c1 == 1 and len(ranked) > 1 and ranked[1][1] == 1:\n            # no locus has >= 2 seeds: ambiguous, unless it looks like a\n            # distant same-strand two-locus (split) read -> verify later\n            (st2x, s2x), c2x = ranked[1]\n            if len(ranked) == 2 and st2x == st1 and abs(s2x - s1) > READ_LEN:\n                pass  # fall through: treat as split candidate\n            else:\n                status[i] = AMBIG\n                continue\n```\nThen the subsequent code sets primary (support 1) and the split check `if len(ranked) > 1:` requires st2 == st1 and abs diff > READ_LEN → marks SPLIT with secondary hit. Good, that falls through correctly. Junction verification will confirm/reject.\n\nNow Part 3. Let's write it.\n\nDepth normalization detail:\n```python\nvalid_start = (bad_cum[READ_LEN:] - bad_cum[:-READ_LEN]) == 0  # length L-READ_LEN+1\n```\nbad_cum = np.cumsum(codes != 4)? no: bad_cum = np.zeros(L+1); bad_cum[1:] = cumsum(codes == 4). valid[p] = bad_cum[p+READ_LEN] - bad_cum[p] == 0, for p in 0..L-READ_LEN.\n\nFine bins for starts: nbins_fine = ceil((L-READ_LEN+1)/FINE_BIN). reads_fine = bincount(starts // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbins_fine). valid_fine = bincount(positions where valid, same binning). cn_fine = (reads_fine/valid_fine) / (total_reads_used/total_valid), with guard for valid>0.\n\nBig bins: aggregate: reads_big = bincount(starts // BIG_BIN), valid_big = bincount(valid positions // BIG_BIN). cn_big similarly.\n\nNote: starts are already filtered to [0, L-READ_LEN].\n\nCandidate run detection on big bins: consider bins with valid_big >= 0.5*BIG_BIN (mappable). cn threshold LOW = 0.35, HET = 0.70. Runs of consecutive mappable bins with cn < LOW. If none, try < HET (heterozygous). Pick longest run (tie: lower cn).\n\nRefinement of boundaries at fine-bin resolution: take the region [run_start_big*BIG_BIN, (run_end_big+1)*BIG_BIN); extend left/right across adjacent fine bins while cn_fine < LOW (only where valid_fine >= 0.5*FINE_BIN). Gives depth_start_bp, depth_end_bp.\n\nDiscordant analysis as planned. Insert stats: spans of FR pairs with both support>=2 and span <= 5000 → median/MAD (1.4826× median absolute deviation).\n\nThreshold: T = max(2000, int(median + 8*mad)).\n\nDiscordant set: span >= T. For each pair: span, D_est = span - median_insert (approximate), midpoint = start1 + span/2.\n\nSplit read verification loop over reads with status==SPLIT:\n```python\nfor i in np.where(status==SPLIT)[0]:\n    ok, blo, bhi, D = verify_split_junction(refc, codes_r[i], start[i], split_start2[i], split_hit_off[i], split_hit_pos[i])\n```\nNote: primary s1 = start[i], secondary info in split arrays. Which side is left? D>0 implies p2 - off2 > s1 → the second locus is downstream → left = s1 side. If D <= READ_LEN → reject (not a large deletion; could be a small variant or misalign).\n\nClustering: list of (blo, D). Sort by blo; greedily merge if blo within 100bp and D within 100bp. Cluster support = count. Best cluster = max support.\n\nRefined breakpoints:\n- If any verified split cluster: refined_start_1b = best.blo + 1, refined_end_1b = best.blo + best.D (last deleted base = blo+D). Precision: single-base (split-read verified).\n- elif discordant: refined_start_1b = min midpoint, end = max midpoint (precision ±fragment length, i.e., ~±300bp).\n- else depth: refined = depth boundaries (precision ±FINE_BIN).\n\nBut: if both depth and splits exist, check consistency: splits should be within the depth region ±1 fine bin. If not consistent, note in report and trust depth for region and splits for breakpoints only if within ±10kb of depth boundary… let's just report the discrepancy.\n\nsize_bp in TSV: rounded size = end_100kb - start_100kb. Include refined size in qc/report.\n\nAlso supporting_signals: include depth bin count and cn, discordant pair count and their median D_est, split read count and their breakpoint.\n\nReport: markdown with sections: Task, Data, Methods, Results (table of signals), Breakpoint evidence vs precision, Final call (rounded + refined), Limitations.\n\nQC JSON: everything.\n\nMain also prints a summary at the end.\n\nOne more detail — read starts counted for depth: include both mates of properly-mapped pairs plus any UNIQUE/SPLIT with support>=2 reads. This double-counts per fragment (both mates), but since it's uniform, doesn't affect relative cn.\n\nAlso compute overall alignment rate: fraction of reads with support>=2.\n\nOK let's write Part 3.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chenyuqiong\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$part3 = @'\"'\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# signals: depth, discordant pairs, split reads\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef depth_profile(starts, codes, L):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read-start depth in FINE_BIN and BIG_BIN windows, CN-normalized.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    n_valid = L - READ_LEN + 1\n    bad_cum = np.zeros(L + 1, dtype=np.int64)\n    bad_cum[1:] = np.cumsum(codes == 4)\n    valid = (bad_cum[READ_LEN:READ_LEN + n_valid] - bad_cum[:n_valid]) == 0\n    vpos = np.nonzero(valid)[0]\n\n    def norm(reads_b, valid_b):\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\", invalid=\\\"ignore\\\"):\n            dens = reads_b.astype(np.float64) / np.maximum(valid_b, 1)\n        scale = starts.size / max(vpos.size, 1)\n        return dens / scale if scale > 0 else dens\n\n    nbf = int(math.ceil(n_valid / FINE_BIN))\n    reads_fine = np.bincount(starts // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbf)\n    valid_fine = np.bincount(vpos // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbf)\n    cn_fine = norm(reads_fine, valid_fine)\n\n    nbb = int(math.ceil(n_valid / BIG_BIN))\n    reads_big = np.bincount(starts // BIG_BIN, minlength=nbb)\n    valid_big = np.bincount(vpos // BIG_BIN, minlength=nbb)\n    cn_big = norm(reads_big, valid_big)\n    mappable_big = valid_big >= 0.5 * BIG_BIN\n    mappable_fine = valid_fine >= 0.5 * FINE_BIN\n    return cn_fine, cn_big, mappable_fine, mappable_big, valid\n\n\ndef find_low_depth_run(cn_big, mappable_big, low):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Longest run of consecutive mappable big bins with cn < low.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    flag = mappable_big & (cn_big < low)\n    best = None\n    i = 0\n    n = len(flag)\n    while i < n:\n        if flag[i]:\n            j = i\n            while j < n and flag[j]:\n                j += 1\n            if best is None or (j - i) > (best[1] - best[0]):\n                best = (i, j)\n            i = j\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return best\n\n\ndef refine_boundaries(cn_fine, mappable_fine, b0, b1, low):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Extend/refine a big-bin run [b0,b1) to fine-bin resolution.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    lo_bin = b0 * BIG_BIN // FINE_BIN\n    hi_bin = int(math.ceil(b1 * BIG_BIN / FINE_BIN))\n    lo_bin = max(lo_bin - 5, 0)\n    hi_bin = min(hi_bin + 5, len(cn_fine))\n    i, j = None, None\n    for x in range(lo_bin, hi_bin):\n        if mappable_fine[x] and cn_fine[x] < low:\n            if i is None:\n                i = x\n            j = x\n    if i is None:\n        return b0 * BIG_BIN, b1 * BIG_BIN\n    return i * FINE_BIN, (j + 1) * FINE_BIN\n\n\ndef main():\n    t_start = time.time()\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    ref_name, ref_seq = load_reference(REF_PATH)\n    L = len(ref_seq)\n    log(f\\\"reference {ref_name}: {L:,} bp\\\")\n    refc = encode(ref_seq.encode())\n    acgt = int((refc \"'!= 4).sum())\n\n    n1, c1 = load_reads(R1_PATH)\n    n2, c2 = load_reads(R2_PATH)\n    assert n1 == n2, f\"mate files not same length: {n1} vs {n2}\"\n    npairs = n1\n    log(f\"loaded {npairs:,} read pairs (read length {READ_LEN})\")\n\n    sh, sp = build_index(refc)\n    a1 = align_reads(c1, sh, sp)\n    a2 = align_reads(c2, sh, sp)\n\n    usable1 = (a1[\"support\"] >= 2)\n    usable2 = (a2[\"support\"] >= 2)\n    aln_rate = (usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()) / (2.0 * npairs)\n    log(f\"alignment: {int(usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()):,}/{2 * npairs:,} \"\n        f\"reads placed with >=2 seeds ({aln_rate:.3%})\")\n\n    # ---------------- read depth ----------------\n    starts_all = np.concatenate([a1[\"start\"][usable1], a2[\"start\"][usable2]])\n    starts_all = starts_all[(starts_all >= 0) & (starts_all <= L - READ_LEN)]\n    cn_fine, cn_big, map_fine, map_big, valid_start = depth_profile(\n        starts_all, refc, L)\n    med_cn = float(np.median(cn_big[map_big]))\n    log(f\"genome-wide median big-bin CN = {med_cn:.3f} \"\n        f\"(mean depth ~ {starts_all.size * READ_LEN / acgt:.2f}x)\")\n\n    LOW_HOM, LOW_HET = 0.35, 0.70\n    run = find_low_depth_run(cn_big, map_big, LOW_HOM)\n    zygosity = \"homozygous-like\"\n    if run is None:\n        run = find_low_depth_run(cn_big, map_big, LOW_HET)\n        zygosity = \"heterozygous-like\"\n    assert run is not None, \"no large low-depth region found\"\n    b0, b1 = run\n    depth_start, depth_end = refine_boundaries(cn_fine, map_fine, b0, b1,\n                                               zygosity[:4] == \"homo\" and LOW_HOM or LOW_HET)\n    n_big_bins = b1 - b0\n    cn_in = float(np.median(cn_big[b0:b1]))\n    outside = np.concatenate([cn_big[:b0], cn_big[b1:]])\n    cn_out = float(np.median(outside[map_big[:b0].sum():]) if False else\n                   np.median(np.concatenate([cn_big[:b0][map_big[:b0]],\n                                             cn_big[b1:][map_big[b1:]]])))\n    log(f\"depth call: {ref_name}:{depth_start:,}-{depth_end:,} \"\n        f\"({n_big_bins} x 100kb bins, CN {cn_in:.3f} vs {cn_out:.3f} outside, \"\n        f\"{zygosity})\")\n\n    # ---------------- discordant pairs ----------------\n    both = usable1 & usable2\n    fr = both & (a1[\"strand\"] == 1) & (a2[\"strand\"] == -1) & '\"\\\\\n        (a2[\\\"start\\\"] >= a1[\\\"start\\\"])\n    spans = (a2[\\\"start\\\"] + READ_LEN - a1[\\\"start\\\"])[fr].astype(np.int64)\n    core = spans[spans <= 5000]\n    ins_med = float(np.median(core)) if core.size else 300.0\n    ins_mad = float(np.median(np.abs(core - ins_med))) * 1.4826 if core.size else 50.0\n    T = max(2000, int(ins_med + 8 * ins_mad))\n    disc_idx = np.nonzero(fr)[0][spans >= T]\n    disc_spans = spans[spans >= T]\n    disc_mid = ((a1[\\\"start\\\"] + (a2[\\\"start\\\"] + READ_LEN) ) / 2.0)[disc_idx]\n    log(f\\\"insert size: median {ins_med:.0f} bp, MAD {ins_mad:.0f} bp; \\\"\n        f\\\"discordant (span >= {T}): {disc_idx.size:,}\\\")\n\n    # ---------------- split reads ----------------\n    splits = []\n    for arr, cd in ((a1, c1), (a2, c2)):\n        idx = np.nonzero(arr[\\\"status\\\"] == SPLIT)[0]\n        for i in idx:\n            ok, blo, bhi, D = verify_split_junction(\n                refc, cd[i], int(arr[\\\"start\\\"][i]), int(arr[\\\"split_start2\\\"][i]),\n                int(arr[\\\"split_hit_off\\\"][i]), int(arr[\\\"split_hit_pos\\\"][i]))\n            if ok:\n                splits.append((blo, bhi, D))\n    splits.sort()\n    clusters = []\n    for blo, bhi, D in splits:\n        if clusters and abs(blo - clusters[-1][\\\"blo\\\"]) <= 100 and \\\\\n                abs(D - clusters[-1][\\\"D\\\"]) <= 100:\n            c = clusters[-1]\n            c[\\\"n\\\"] += 1\n            c[\\\"blo\\\"] = min(c[\\\"blo\\\"], blo)\n            c[\\\"bhi\\\"] = max(c[\\\"bhi\\\"], bhi)\n        else:\n            clusters.append(dict(blo=blo, bhi=bhi, D=D, n=1))\n    if clusters:\n        best = max(clusters, key=lambda c: c[\\\"n\\\"])\n        log(f\\\"split reads verified: {len(splits)} \\\"\n            f\\\"({len(clusters)} junction cluster(s); best n={best['n']})\\\")\n\n    # ---------------- integrate ----------------\n    if clusters:\n        refined_start = best[\\\"blo\\\"] + 1            # 1-based first deleted base\n        refined_end = best[\\\"blo\\\"] + best[\\\"D\\\"]      # 1-based last deleted base\n        refined_method = \\\"split_reads\\\"\n        refined_precision = \\\"single-base (verified junction)\\\"\n    elif disc_idx.size:\n        refined_start = int(disc_mid.min())\n        refined_end = int(disc_mid.max())\n        refined_method = \\\"discordant_pairs\\\"\n        refined_precision = f\\\"~fragment length (+/- {int(ins_med)} bp)\\\"\n    else:\n        refined_start = depth_start + 1\n        refined_end = depth_end\n        refined_method = \\\"read_depth\\\"\n        refined_precision = f\\\"~{FINE_BIN // 1000} kb (depth bin)\\\"\n\n    s100 = round_half_up_100kb(refined_start)\n    e100 = round_half_up_100kb(refined_end)\n    if e100 <= s100:\n        e100 = s100 + BIG_BIN\n    size100 = e100 - s100\n    size_refined = refined_end - refined_start + 1\n\n    signals = []\n    signals.append(\n        f\\\"read_depth={n_big_bins} consecutive 100kb bins with CN \\\"\n        f\\\"{cn_in:.2f} vs {cn_out:.2f} genome median ({zygosity}); \\\"\n        f\\\"depth interval {ref_name}:{depth_start + 1}-{depth_end}\\\")\n    if disc_idx.size:\n        signals.append(\n            f\\\"discordant_pairs={disc_idx.size} FR pairs with span >= {T} \\\"\n            f\\\"(median span {int(np.median(disc_spans)):,} bp)\\\")\n    if clusters:\n        signals.append(\n            f\\\"split_reads={len(splits)} verified across \\\"\n            f\\\"{len(clusters)} junction cluster(s) at ~{ref_name}:\\\"\n            f\\\"{best['blo'] + 1}\\\")\n    supporting = \\\" | \\\".join(signals)\n\n    # ---------------- outputs ----------------\n    tsv_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"deletion.tsv\\\")\n    with open(tsv_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        fh.write(\\\"chrom\\\\tstart_100kb\\\\tend_100kb\\\\tsize_bp\\\\tsupporting_signals\\\\n\\\")\n        fh.write(f\\\"{ref_name}\\\\t{s100}\\\\t{e100}\\\\t{size100}\\\\t{supporting}\\\\n\\\")\n    log(f\\\"wrote {tsv_path}\\\")\n\n    qc = {\n        \\\"reference\\\": {\\\"name\\\": ref_name, \\\"length_bp\\\": L, \\\"acgt_bp\\\": acgt},\n        \\\"reads\\\": {\n            \\\"pairs\\\": npairs, \\\"read_length\\\": READ_LEN,\n            \\\"aligned_reads_with_2plus_seeds\\\": int(usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()),\n            \\\"alignment_rate\\\": round(aln_rate, 4),\n            \\\"mean_genome_depth_x\\\": round(starts_all.size * READ_LEN / acgt, 3),\n        },\n        \\\"insert_size\\\": {\\\"median_bp\\\": round(ins_med, 1),\n                        \\\"mad_bp\\\": round(ins_mad, 1),\n                        \\\"discordant_threshold_bp\\\": T},\n        \\\"deletion\\\": {\n            \\\"chrom\\\": ref_name,\n            \\\"zygosity_call\\\": zygosity,\n            \\\"depth_region_1based\\\": {\\\"start\\\": depth_start + 1, \\\"end\\\": depth_end},\n            \\\"depth_cn_inside\\\": round(cn_in, 4),\n            \\\"depth_cn_outside\\\": round(cn_out, 4),\n            \\\"depth_big_bins_below_threshold\\\": n_big_bins,\n            \\\"discordant_pairs\\\": int(disc_idx.size),\n            \\\"split_reads_verified\\\": len(splits),\n            \\\"split_clusters\\\": [\n                {\\\"left_breakpoint_1based\\\": c[\\\"blo\\\"] + 1,\n                 \\\"breakpoint_uncertainty_bp\\\": c[\\\"bhi\\\"] - c[\\\"blo\\\"],\n                 \\\"size_bp\\\": c[\\\"D\\\"], \\\"support\\\": c[\\\"n\\\"]} for c in clusters],\n            \\\"refined_start_1based\\\": refined_start,\n            \\\"refined_end_1based\\\": refined_end,\n            \\\"refined_size_bp\\\": size_refined,\n            \\\"refined_method\\\": refined_method,\n            \\\"refined_precision\\\": refined_precision,\n            \\\"reported_start_100kb\\\": s100,\n            \\\"reported_end_100kb\\\": e100,\n            \\\"reported_size_bp\\\": size100,\n        },\n        \\\"runtime_seconds\\\": round(time.time() - t_start, 1),\n    }\n    qc_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"qc.json\\\")\n    with open(qc_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        json.dump(qc, fh, indent=2)\n    log(f\\\"wrote {qc_path}\\\")\n\n    report = build_report(qc, cn_big, map_big, b0, b1, clusters, disc_idx,\n                          disc_spans, supporting)\n    md_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"report.md\\\")\n    with open(md_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        fh.write(report)\n    log(f\\\"wrote {md_path}\\\")\n    log(\\\"done\\\")\n\n\ndef build_report(qc, cn_big, map_big, b0, b1, clusters, disc_idx, disc_spans,\n                 supporting):\n    d = qc[\\\"deletion\\\"]\n    prof = \\\", \\\".join(\n        f\\\"{i * BIG_BIN // 1000}kb:{cn_big[i]:.2f}\\\"\n        for i in range(max(b0 - 2, 0), min(b1 + 2, len(cn_big)))\n        if map_big[i])\n    split_txt = \\\"none\\\"\n    if clusters:\n        split_txt = \\\"; \\\".join(\n            f\\\"junction at ~{c['blo'] + 1:,} (size {c['D']:,} bp, {c['n']} read(s))\\\"\n            for c in clusters)\n    disc_txt = \\\"none\\\"\n    if disc_idx.size:\n        disc_txt = (f\\\"{disc_idx.size} FR pair(s) with span >= \\\"\n                    f\\\"{qc['insert_size']['discordant_threshold_bp']}, \\\"\n                    f\\\"median span {int(np.median(disc_spans)):,} bp\\\")\n    return f\\\"\\\"\\\"# Large deletion call - shallow PE hg38 (chr22)\n\n## Data\n- Reference: \"'`{qc['\"'reference']['name']}\"'` ({qc['\"'reference']['length_bp']:,} bp,\n  {qc['reference']['acgt_bp']:,} ACGT bp).\n- Reads: {qc['reads']['pairs']:,} paired-end x {qc['reads']['read_length']} bp\n  (~{qc['reads']['mean_genome_depth_x']}x mean depth, shallow).\n- Alignment (exact 25-mer seed index, no external aligner):\n  {qc['reads']['aligned_reads_with_2plus_seeds']:,} reads placed with >= 2\n  consistent seeds ({qc['reads']['alignment_rate']:.1%}).\n- Insert size: median {qc['insert_size']['median_bp']:.0f} bp\n  (MAD {qc['insert_size']['mad_bp']:.0f} bp).\n\n## Signals used (independent evidence)\n1. **Read depth** - 100 kb bins, normalized by per-bin mappable sequence.\n   {d['depth_big_bins_below_threshold']} consecutive bins collapse to\n   CN {d['depth_cn_inside']:.2f} vs {d['depth_cn_outside']:.2f} elsewhere\n   ({d['zygosity_call']}). Depth path around the call (bin:CN): {prof}.\n2. **Discordant pairs** - {disc_txt}.\n3. **Split reads** - {split_txt}.\n\n## Call\n| item | value |\n|---|---|\n| chrom | {d['chrom']} |\n| depth-only interval (1-based) | {d['depth_region_1based']['start']:,} - {d['depth_region_1based']['end']:,} |\n| refined breakpoints (1-based) | {d['refined_start_1based']:,} - {d['refined_end_1based']:,} |\n| refined size | {d['refined_size_bp']:,} bp |\n| refined by | {d['refined_method']} ({d['refined_precision']}) |\n| **reported start (rounded 100 kb)** | **{d['reported_start_100kb']:,}** |\n| **reported end (rounded 100 kb)** | **{d['reported_end_100kb']:,}** |\n| **reported size** | **{d['reported_size_bp']:,} bp** |\n\n## Evidence vs precision\n- The rounded coordinates in \"'`deletion.tsv` are limited to the task'\"'s\n  mandated 100 kb grid; rounding is half-up on each breakpoint.\n- Read depth alone localizes each breakpoint only to ~10 kb (fine bin) plus\n  sampling noise; it establishes the interval and zygosity.\n- Discordant pairs narrow a breakpoint to roughly one fragment length\n  (~{qc['insert_size']['median_bp']:.0f} bp).\n- Verified split reads give single-base breakpoints; where present they are\n  the evidence behind the refined coordinates, and the 100 kb values above\n  are a reporting convention, not the measurement precision.\n\n## Supporting signals (verbatim in deletion.tsv)\n{supporting}\n\n_Generated by output/analysis.py in {qc['runtime_seconds']} s._\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\n\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\n    main()\n'@\nAdd-Content -LiteralPath output\\\\analysis.py -Value \"'$part3 -Encoding utf8\nWrite-Host \"part3 appended, lines: $((Get-Content output'\"\\\\analysis.py).Count)\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chenyuqiong\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$part3 = @'\"'\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# signals: depth, discordant pairs, split reads\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef depth_profile(starts, codes, L):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read-start depth in FINE_BIN and BIG_BIN windows, CN-normalized.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    n_valid = L - READ_LEN + 1\n    bad_cum = np.zeros(L + 1, dtype=np.int64)\n    bad_cum[1:] = np.cumsum(codes == 4)\n    valid = (bad_cum[READ_LEN:READ_LEN + n_valid] - bad_cum[:n_valid]) == 0\n    vpos = np.nonzero(valid)[0]\n\n    def norm(reads_b, valid_b):\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\", invalid=\\\"ignore\\\"):\n            dens = reads_b.astype(np.float64) / np.maximum(valid_b, 1)\n        scale = starts.size / max(vpos.size, 1)\n        return dens / scale if scale > 0 else dens\n\n    nbf = int(math.ceil(n_valid / FINE_BIN))\n    reads_fine = np.bincount(starts // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbf)\n    valid_fine = np.bincount(vpos // FINE_BIN, minlength=nbf)\n    cn_fine = norm(reads_fine, valid_fine)\n\n    nbb = int(math.ceil(n_valid / BIG_BIN))\n    reads_big = np.bincount(starts // BIG_BIN, minlength=nbb)\n    valid_big = np.bincount(vpos // BIG_BIN, minlength=nbb)\n    cn_big = norm(reads_big, valid_big)\n    mappable_big = valid_big >= 0.5 * BIG_BIN\n    mappable_fine = valid_fine >= 0.5 * FINE_BIN\n    return cn_fine, cn_big, mappable_fine, mappable_big, valid\n\n\ndef find_low_depth_run(cn_big, mappable_big, low):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Longest run of consecutive mappable big bins with cn < low.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    flag = mappable_big & (cn_big < low)\n    best = None\n    i = 0\n    n = len(flag)\n    while i < n:\n        if flag[i]:\n            j = i\n            while j < n and flag[j]:\n                j += 1\n            if best is None or (j - i) > (best[1] - best[0]):\n                best = (i, j)\n            i = j\n        else:\n            i += 1\n    return best\n\n\ndef refine_boundaries(cn_fine, mappable_fine, b0, b1, low):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Extend/refine a big-bin run [b0,b1) to fine-bin resolution.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    lo_bin = b0 * BIG_BIN // FINE_BIN\n    hi_bin = int(math.ceil(b1 * BIG_BIN / FINE_BIN))\n    lo_bin = max(lo_bin - 5, 0)\n    hi_bin = min(hi_bin + 5, len(cn_fine))\n    i, j = None, None\n    for x in range(lo_bin, hi_bin):\n        if mappable_fine[x] and cn_fine[x] < low:\n            if i is None:\n                i = x\n            j = x\n    if i is None:\n        return b0 * BIG_BIN, b1 * BIG_BIN\n    return i * FINE_BIN, (j + 1) * FINE_BIN\n\n\ndef main():\n    t_start = time.time()\n    os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    ref_name, ref_seq = load_reference(REF_PATH)\n    L = len(ref_seq)\n    log(f\\\"reference {ref_name}: {L:,} bp\\\")\n    refc = encode(ref_seq.encode())\n    acgt = int((refc \"'!= 4).sum())\n\n    n1, c1 = load_reads(R1_PATH)\n    n2, c2 = load_reads(R2_PATH)\n    assert n1 == n2, f\"mate files not same length: {n1} vs {n2}\"\n    npairs = n1\n    log(f\"loaded {npairs:,} read pairs (read length {READ_LEN})\")\n\n    sh, sp = build_index(refc)\n    a1 = align_reads(c1, sh, sp)\n    a2 = align_reads(c2, sh, sp)\n\n    usable1 = (a1[\"support\"] >= 2)\n    usable2 = (a2[\"support\"] >= 2)\n    aln_rate = (usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()) / (2.0 * npairs)\n    log(f\"alignment: {int(usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()):,}/{2 * npairs:,} \"\n        f\"reads placed with >=2 seeds ({aln_rate:.3%})\")\n\n    # ---------------- read depth ----------------\n    starts_all = np.concatenate([a1[\"start\"][usable1], a2[\"start\"][usable2]])\n    starts_all = starts_all[(starts_all >= 0) & (starts_all <= L - READ_LEN)]\n    cn_fine, cn_big, map_fine, map_big, valid_start = depth_profile(\n        starts_all, refc, L)\n    med_cn = float(np.median(cn_big[map_big]))\n    log(f\"genome-wide median big-bin CN = {med_cn:.3f} \"\n        f\"(mean depth ~ {starts_all.size * READ_LEN / acgt:.2f}x)\")\n\n    LOW_HOM, LOW_HET = 0.35, 0.70\n    run = find_low_depth_run(cn_big, map_big, LOW_HOM)\n    zygosity = \"homozygous-like\"\n    if run is None:\n        run = find_low_depth_run(cn_big, map_big, LOW_HET)\n        zygosity = \"heterozygous-like\"\n    assert run is not None, \"no large low-depth region found\"\n    b0, b1 = run\n    depth_start, depth_end = refine_boundaries(cn_fine, map_fine, b0, b1,\n                                               zygosity[:4] == \"homo\" and LOW_HOM or LOW_HET)\n    n_big_bins = b1 - b0\n    cn_in = float(np.median(cn_big[b0:b1]))\n    outside = np.concatenate([cn_big[:b0], cn_big[b1:]])\n    cn_out = float(np.median(outside[map_big[:b0].sum():]) if False else\n                   np.median(np.concatenate([cn_big[:b0][map_big[:b0]],\n                                             cn_big[b1:][map_big[b1:]]])))\n    log(f\"depth call: {ref_name}:{depth_start:,}-{depth_end:,} \"\n        f\"({n_big_bins} x 100kb bins, CN {cn_in:.3f} vs {cn_out:.3f} outside, \"\n        f\"{zygosity})\")\n\n    # ---------------- discordant pairs ----------------\n    both = usable1 & usable2\n    fr = both & (a1[\"strand\"] == 1) & (a2[\"strand\"] == -1) & '\"\\\\\n        (a2[\\\"start\\\"] >= a1[\\\"start\\\"])\n    spans = (a2[\\\"start\\\"] + READ_LEN - a1[\\\"start\\\"])[fr].astype(np.int64)\n    core = spans[spans <= 5000]\n    ins_med = float(np.median(core)) if core.size else 300.0\n    ins_mad = float(np.median(np.abs(core - ins_med))) * 1.4826 if core.size else 50.0\n    T = max(2000, int(ins_med + 8 * ins_mad))\n    disc_idx = np.nonzero(fr)[0][spans >= T]\n    disc_spans = spans[spans >= T]\n    disc_mid = ((a1[\\\"start\\\"] + (a2[\\\"start\\\"] + READ_LEN) ) / 2.0)[disc_idx]\n    log(f\\\"insert size: median {ins_med:.0f} bp, MAD {ins_mad:.0f} bp; \\\"\n        f\\\"discordant (span >= {T}): {disc_idx.size:,}\\\")\n\n    # ---------------- split reads ----------------\n    splits = []\n    for arr, cd in ((a1, c1), (a2, c2)):\n        idx = np.nonzero(arr[\\\"status\\\"] == SPLIT)[0]\n        for i in idx:\n            ok, blo, bhi, D = verify_split_junction(\n                refc, cd[i], int(arr[\\\"start\\\"][i]), int(arr[\\\"split_start2\\\"][i]),\n                int(arr[\\\"split_hit_off\\\"][i]), int(arr[\\\"split_hit_pos\\\"][i]))\n            if ok:\n                splits.append((blo, bhi, D))\n    splits.sort()\n    clusters = []\n    for blo, bhi, D in splits:\n        if clusters and abs(blo - clusters[-1][\\\"blo\\\"]) <= 100 and \\\\\n                abs(D - clusters[-1][\\\"D\\\"]) <= 100:\n            c = clusters[-1]\n            c[\\\"n\\\"] += 1\n            c[\\\"blo\\\"] = min(c[\\\"blo\\\"], blo)\n            c[\\\"bhi\\\"] = max(c[\\\"bhi\\\"], bhi)\n        else:\n            clusters.append(dict(blo=blo, bhi=bhi, D=D, n=1))\n    if clusters:\n        best = max(clusters, key=lambda c: c[\\\"n\\\"])\n        log(f\\\"split reads verified: {len(splits)} \\\"\n            f\\\"({len(clusters)} junction cluster(s); best n={best['n']})\\\")\n\n    # ---------------- integrate ----------------\n    if clusters:\n        refined_start = best[\\\"blo\\\"] + 1            # 1-based first deleted base\n        refined_end = best[\\\"blo\\\"] + best[\\\"D\\\"]      # 1-based last deleted base\n        refined_method = \\\"split_reads\\\"\n        refined_precision = \\\"single-base (verified junction)\\\"\n    elif disc_idx.size:\n        refined_start = int(disc_mid.min())\n        refined_end = int(disc_mid.max())\n        refined_method = \\\"discordant_pairs\\\"\n        refined_precision = f\\\"~fragment length (+/- {int(ins_med)} bp)\\\"\n    else:\n        refined_start = depth_start + 1\n        refined_end = depth_end\n        refined_method = \\\"read_depth\\\"\n        refined_precision = f\\\"~{FINE_BIN // 1000} kb (depth bin)\\\"\n\n    s100 = round_half_up_100kb(refined_start)\n    e100 = round_half_up_100kb(refined_end)\n    if e100 <= s100:\n        e100 = s100 + BIG_BIN\n    size100 = e100 - s100\n    size_refined = refined_end - refined_start + 1\n\n    signals = []\n    signals.append(\n        f\\\"read_depth={n_big_bins} consecutive 100kb bins with CN \\\"\n        f\\\"{cn_in:.2f} vs {cn_out:.2f} genome median ({zygosity}); \\\"\n        f\\\"depth interval {ref_name}:{depth_start + 1}-{depth_end}\\\")\n    if disc_idx.size:\n        signals.append(\n            f\\\"discordant_pairs={disc_idx.size} FR pairs with span >= {T} \\\"\n            f\\\"(median span {int(np.median(disc_spans)):,} bp)\\\")\n    if clusters:\n        signals.append(\n            f\\\"split_reads={len(splits)} verified across \\\"\n            f\\\"{len(clusters)} junction cluster(s) at ~{ref_name}:\\\"\n            f\\\"{best['blo'] + 1}\\\")\n    supporting = \\\" | \\\".join(signals)\n\n    # ---------------- outputs ----------------\n    tsv_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"deletion.tsv\\\")\n    with open(tsv_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        fh.write(\\\"chrom\\\\tstart_100kb\\\\tend_100kb\\\\tsize_bp\\\\tsupporting_signals\\\\n\\\")\n        fh.write(f\\\"{ref_name}\\\\t{s100}\\\\t{e100}\\\\t{size100}\\\\t{supporting}\\\\n\\\")\n    log(f\\\"wrote {tsv_path}\\\")\n\n    qc = {\n        \\\"reference\\\": {\\\"name\\\": ref_name, \\\"length_bp\\\": L, \\\"acgt_bp\\\": acgt},\n        \\\"reads\\\": {\n            \\\"pairs\\\": npairs, \\\"read_length\\\": READ_LEN,\n            \\\"aligned_reads_with_2plus_seeds\\\": int(usable1.sum() + usable2.sum()),\n            \\\"alignment_rate\\\": round(aln_rate, 4),\n            \\\"mean_genome_depth_x\\\": round(starts_all.size * READ_LEN / acgt, 3),\n        },\n        \\\"insert_size\\\": {\\\"median_bp\\\": round(ins_med, 1),\n                        \\\"mad_bp\\\": round(ins_mad, 1),\n                        \\\"discordant_threshold_bp\\\": T},\n        \\\"deletion\\\": {\n            \\\"chrom\\\": ref_name,\n            \\\"zygosity_call\\\": zygosity,\n            \\\"depth_region_1based\\\": {\\\"start\\\": depth_start + 1, \\\"end\\\": depth_end},\n            \\\"depth_cn_inside\\\": round(cn_in, 4),\n            \\\"depth_cn_outside\\\": round(cn_out, 4),\n            \\\"depth_big_bins_below_threshold\\\": n_big_bins,\n            \\\"discordant_pairs\\\": int(disc_idx.size),\n            \\\"split_reads_verified\\\": len(splits),\n            \\\"split_clusters\\\": [\n                {\\\"left_breakpoint_1based\\\": c[\\\"blo\\\"] + 1,\n                 \\\"breakpoint_uncertainty_bp\\\": c[\\\"bhi\\\"] - c[\\\"blo\\\"],\n                 \\\"size_bp\\\": c[\\\"D\\\"], \\\"support\\\": c[\\\"n\\\"]} for c in clusters],\n            \\\"refined_start_1based\\\": refined_start,\n            \\\"refined_end_1based\\\": refined_end,\n            \\\"refined_size_bp\\\": size_refined,\n            \\\"refined_method\\\": refined_method,\n            \\\"refined_precision\\\": refined_precision,\n            \\\"reported_start_100kb\\\": s100,\n            \\\"reported_end_100kb\\\": e100,\n            \\\"reported_size_bp\\\": size100,\n        },\n        \\\"runtime_seconds\\\": round(time.time() - t_start, 1),\n    }\n    qc_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"qc.json\\\")\n    with open(qc_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        json.dump(qc, fh, indent=2)\n    log(f\\\"wrote {qc_path}\\\")\n\n    report = build_report(qc, cn_big, map_big, b0, b1, clusters, disc_idx,\n                          disc_spans, supporting)\n    md_path = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"report.md\\\")\n    with open(md_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\n        fh.write(report)\n    log(f\\\"wrote {md_path}\\\")\n    log(\\\"done\\\")\n\n\ndef build_report(qc, cn_big, map_big, b0, b1, clusters, disc_idx, disc_spans